{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider contests the whole SGD 33.17, but this category's remedy is arithmetic and comes to much less. On the platform's own fare ledger, charged_total is SGD 33.17 and the recomputed_fare on the booked optimal route is SGD 15.57 (SGD 3.80 base + SGD 7.05 distance + SGD 3.92 time at the fare_breakdown surge_multiplier of 1.0 + SGD 0.80 platform fee, no ERP, no promo), so the refund under POL-RD-02 is exactly SGD 17.60 — 53.06% of the amount charged and well short of the 90% share at which POL-RD-02 converts the outcome to a full refund. The driver keeps the SGD 15.57 the trip was worth on the optimal route; no more than SGD 17.60 moves, and the 'nearly three times the normal price' in the claim is not a measure of anything the policy refunds.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00504", "EV-TRIP-00504"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is properly triggered by the material deviation, but it produces nothing against this driver. The excess is 14.46 km and 153.83% of the 9.4 km optimal route, against POL-RD-01's material figures of 8.0 km and 50%, so the check must be run; on the only two fields POL-RD-06 permits, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 250, and neither limb of the pattern test is met (0 is below 3, and 0/250 is 0.00 against the 0.05 ratio with the 40-trip minimum satisfied). There is therefore no FULL_REFUND uplift of charged_total under POL-RD-06(b) and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c): the remedy stays at the ordinary POL-RD-02 partial figure. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter, and every other field on the profile, may not be substituted for the trailing-90-day figure under POL-GEN-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00504", "EV-GPS-00504"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing is added on top of the distance-and-time refund. The fare ledger carries no ERP or toll lines at all — off-optimal-route total SGD 0.00 and on-optimal-route total SGD 0.00 — and its airport_surcharge line is SGD 0.00, so the standalone pass-through correction POL-RD-09 provides for off-route gantries and wrongly applied surcharges is nil on this trip. Under POL-RD-09(1) any off-route ERP would in any event already be comprehended in the POL-RD-02 refund and must never be added to it a second time. The rider's recovery is the distance-and-time differential and nothing else.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00504"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's account — a car behind him flashing high beams near the exit, an expected accident ahead, staying on the expressway and turning back at the next exit — is on the file, but this brief does not claim it exonerates him, because on this record it cannot. The only traffic advisory for the trip, EV-ADVIS-00504-01, is MISSING, carrying admissibility weight 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT: no advisory covers the PIE eastbound between Paya Lebar and Tampines in this window. Under POL-RD-13 a traffic assertion is tested against the trip's advisory and nothing else; that comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. No part of the 14.46 km excess is therefore excluded, and the excess stands at the measured figure. For completeness, the trace that measures it is not impaired under POL-RD-07 — 229 fixes at a 10 s interval against a 10 s expected interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00504-01", "EV-GPS-00504"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}
